# Apple Silicon, streaming recogniser: NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 ASR streaming 0.6B (8-bit MLX) for English, German, Czech... sources; Slovak sources use the Slovak Whisper fine-tune.
# MEASURED on this 16 GB M1 Pro, generated English (en_paced, 60 s), real route, one run each, scored 2026-11-10 (documentation/evidence/2026-11-09, scripts/live/score_success.py):
#   en->de median lag 0.55 s (p90 2.0 s), en->sk 0.62 s (2.1 s), en->cs 1.2-1.8 s (2.3-2.8 s); early start 88-100%; drift within +-0.5 s/min in every English-source run
#   (the earlier drift "failures" were a last-minus-first lag artefact plus a wall-clock span bug, both fixed 2026-11-10); recogniser word error 5.2%.
# NOT yet measured: real (non-generated) speech, the 2 s goal on Czech output, and the voice speed-up by ear. Needs `pip install --no-deps mlx-audio==0.6.4` in .venv (first run downloads the model).
# Slovak input is NOT served by Nemotron (41% word error): Slovak sources fall back to Whisper + BP_SK_STT_MODEL (about 2.8 s at 6% on generated Slovak, T4 simulation).
# Optional, measured faster but unchecked by ear: BP_RATE_MIN=0.7 (lets the voice speed up to 1.4x; en->sk median lag 0.51 s, en->cs 1.07 s). Run: make run PRESET=mac-nemotron
BP_STT_ENGINE=nemotron
BP_SK_STT_MODEL=ct2_models/whisper-large-v3-turbo-sk
BP_PROSODY=1
BP_LOG_SESSIONS=1
BP_DEFAULT_STRATEGY=agree_short
